{
  "title": "Places in town and directions",
  "note": "Three place particles: に marks a destination or where something exists (駅に行きます, 駅にあります); へ (read e) marks a direction of movement (日本へ行きます); で marks where an action happens (図書館で本を読みます). With 行きます, に and へ are both fine.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Tae Kim's Guide: Particles used with verbs (に, へ, で)",
    "u": "https://guidetojapanese.org/learn/grammar/verbparticles"
  },
